---
title: "Compact Permission Algebra with stdlib/bitset"
author: na-op
date: 2026-11-17
abstract: Pack integer flags across 32-bit words with stdlib/bitset.ltl, compose RBAC roles via set algebra, and verify multi-word boundaries with pinned vectors.
---

## Representation

`stdlib/bitset.ltl` stores a fixed-capacity bitset `[capacity, word_0, word_1, ...]` where each word
packs 32 flags (`num_words = idiv(capacity + 31, 32)`). Out-of-range indices (`pos < 0` or `pos >= capacity`)
are safely ignored by `set` and `clear`, and return `false` in `test`.

## Core Operations & Set Algebra

- **Point updates:** `set(bs, pos)`, `clear(bs, pos)`, `toggle(bs, pos)`, and `test(bs, pos)`.
- **Algebra across words:** `union`, `intersection`, `difference`, `symmetric_difference`, and `is_subset` combine two bitsets across 32-bit word boundaries.
- **Inspection:** `capacity(bs)`, `count(bs)`, `is_empty(bs)`, `to_list(bs)`, `to_binary_string(bs)`, and `to_string(bs)`.

## Runnable Example (`examples/bitset_rbac.ltl`)

```lateralus
// Run from checkout with: python3 scripts/run_bitset_tutorial.py
// Models compact RBAC permission sets across two 32-bit words (capacity = 64).

fn main() {
    // 0=READ, 1=WRITE, 2=DEPLOY, 33=AUDIT_LOG, 40=BILLING_ADMIN
    let role_editor = from_list(64, [0, 1])
    let role_ops = from_list(64, [0, 2, 33])

    let combined = union(role_editor, role_ops)
    let shared = intersection(role_editor, role_ops)
    let ops_only = difference(role_ops, role_editor)
    let xor_perms = symmetric_difference(role_editor, role_ops)

    println("cap=" + str(capacity(combined)))
    println("combined=" + to_string(combined))
    println("shared=" + to_string(shared))
    println("ops_only=" + to_string(ops_only))
    println("xor=" + to_string(xor_perms))
    println("editor_subset_combined=" + str(is_subset(role_editor, combined)))
    println("ops_subset_editor=" + str(is_subset(role_ops, role_editor)))

    // Grant temporary BILLING_ADMIN (40), verify, then toggle off
    let elevated = set(combined, 40)
    println("has_40_after_set=" + str(test(elevated, 40)))
    let revoked = toggle(elevated, 40)
    println("has_40_after_toggle=" + str(test(revoked, 40)))
}
```

## Pinned Test Vector (`examples/bitset_rbac.expected.txt`)

```
cap=64
combined=Bitset([0, 1, 2, 33])
shared=Bitset([0])
ops_only=Bitset([2, 33])
xor=Bitset([1, 2, 33])
editor_subset_combined=True
ops_subset_editor=False
has_40_after_set=True
has_40_after_toggle=False
```
